"citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c2"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c2"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c2","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.68 (Infinitely many greedy skips suffice)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.68, p. 63, label record:257bm-c2","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Suppose that the greedy remainder for $1/2$ satisfies\n$$\n\\forall N\\ \\exists c\\ge\\max\\{N,4\\}:\\qquad\n 0<r_{c-1}(1/2)<w_c.\n$$\nThen exact quotient rows exist at unbounded depths, and $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$. A single such skip at $c$ gives an exact row at depth $2c-2$ without an additional capacity hypothesis. Taking arbitrarily large $c$ therefore supplies the rows needed for the compactness implication in Theorem 6.67. The existence of arbitrarily late positive skips is the hypothesis, not an established property of the greedy sequence. It is equivalent to half-membership and remains unproved here.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c2","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c2","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c2%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c2%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.CofinalExactLocalMersenneHalfRows"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c2","id":"sha256:264b08973a5